{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q418792","formula":"C₁₂H₂₃NO₃","hill":"C12H23NO3","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":12.0,"H":23.0,"N":1.0,"O":3.0},"names":{"en":"Icaridin","ru":"Пикаридин"},"descriptions":{"en":"Picaridin, also known as icaridin, is an insect repellent that can be used directly on skin or clothing. It has broad efficacy against various arthropods such as mosquitos, ticks, gnats, flies and fleas, and is almost colorless and odorless. A study performed in 2010 showed that picaridin spray and cream at the 20% concentration provided 12 hours of protection against ticks.","ru":"Пикаридин (также известен как икаридин) — химическое соединение, репеллент против насекомых с химической формулой C12H23NO3. Можно наносить непосредственно на кожу или одежду. Он обладает широкой эффективностью против различных членистоногих, таких как комары, клещи, мошки, мухи и блохи, и почти не имеет цвета и запаха."},"fame":20,"pubchemCid":125098,"mass":229.32,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCC(C)OC(=O)N1CCCCC1CCO","inchikey":"QLHULAHOXSSASE-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"butan-2-yl 2-(2-hydroxyethyl)piperidine-1-carboxylate","classes":[{"qid":"Q59199015","names":{"en":"group of stereoisomers","ru":"группа стереоизомеров","uk":"група стереоізомерів"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"125098","atoms":39,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.277,"y":-0.632,"z":-0.051,"el":"O"},{"x":2.197,"y":-3.432,"z":0.555,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.046,"y":0.496,"z":1.923,"el":"O"},{"x":0.686,"y":0.507,"z":0.366,"el":"N"},{"x":1.288,"y":-0.077,"z":-0.852,"el":"C"},{"x":2.071,"y":0.976,"z":-1.65,"el":"C"},{"x":3.031,"y":1.785,"z":-0.783,"el":"C"},{"x":2.286,"y":2.404,"z":0.393,"el":"C"},{"x":1.552,"y":1.342,"z":1.203,"el":"C"},{"x":2.145,"y":-1.296,"z":-0.5,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.587,"y":0.152,"z":0.835,"el":"C"},{"x":1.34,"y":-2.342,"z":0.246,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.704,"y":-0.511,"z":-0.025,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.089,"y":0.938,"z":-0.331,"